<map version="1.0.1">
<node ID="ID_2503" TEXT="Chapter 8 — Practice exams and final revision"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>2026-10-26 → 2026-11-02</p><p>All domains</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2396" TEXT="🎯 Goal"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Three practice exams at 80%+, every domain above 75%, cheat sheet internalised, logistics done.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2465" TEXT="📅 Daily plan"><node ID="ID_2405" TEXT="10-26 · Partner Academy official prep course — all quizzes"><node ID="ID_2397" TEXT="Learn: Partner Academy official prep course — all quizzes"></node><node ID="ID_2401" TEXT="Build: Fix weak-domain notes"><node ID="ID_2398" TEXT="Work through the official prep course end to end; take every quiz; note the wording style of questions."></node><node ID="ID_2399" TEXT="For each quiz miss, add a trap line to the matching chapter's My notes."></node><node ID="ID_2400" TEXT="Re-read the Exam Guide task statements; tick each you can teach in one sentence; the unticked ones are tomorrow's focus."></node></node><node ID="ID_2402" TEXT="✔ Done when: Course complete; every task statement ticked or listed as a gap."></node><node ID="ID_2404" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2403" TEXT="Partner Academy prep course" LINK="https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2414" TEXT="10-27 · Practice exam #2 (timed)"><node ID="ID_2406" TEXT="Learn: Practice exam #2 (timed)"></node><node ID="ID_2410" TEXT="Build: Score per domain"><node ID="ID_2407" TEXT="Fresh 53-question set (do not reuse #1); 120-minute timer; flag-and-move-on discipline."></node><node ID="ID_2408" TEXT="Enter per-domain scores in the dashboard (Practice exam 2)."></node><node ID="ID_2409" TEXT="Review misses against docs only after entering the score."></node></node><node ID="ID_2411" TEXT="✔ Done when: Scores entered; every miss cited to a docs sentence."></node><node ID="ID_2413" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2412" TEXT="Free practice questions" LINK="https://claudecertificationguide.com/developer-foundations"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://claudecertificationguide.com/developer-foundations</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2423" TEXT="10-28 · Gap day: rebuild any lab from a domain under 75%"><node ID="ID_2415" TEXT="Learn: Gap day: rebuild any lab from a domain under 75%"></node><node ID="ID_2419" TEXT="Build: Re-read that chapter's traps"><node ID="ID_2416" TEXT="Open the Domain dashboard; pick the lowest domain."></node><node ID="ID_2417" TEXT="Rebuild that chapter's main lab from scratch in 45 minutes with Claude Code, narrating the concepts aloud."></node><node ID="ID_2418" TEXT="Redo that chapter's Self-check and domain quiz; re-read its Study material."></node></node><node ID="ID_2420" TEXT="✔ Done when: Weakest domain quiz retaken at 80%+."></node><node ID="ID_2422" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2421" TEXT="The chapter(s) the dashboard flags"></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2432" TEXT="10-29 · Practice exam #3 (timed)"><node ID="ID_2424" TEXT="Learn: Practice exam #3 (timed)"></node><node ID="ID_2428" TEXT="Build: Score per domain"><node ID="ID_2425" TEXT="Third fresh set; timed; enter scores (Practice exam 3)."></node><node ID="ID_2426" TEXT="Compare the three exams in the dashboard — trend should be up in every domain."></node><node ID="ID_2427" TEXT="If any domain is still under 75%, schedule it for tomorrow's reading."></node></node><node ID="ID_2429" TEXT="✔ Done when: Scores entered; trend reviewed."></node><node ID="ID_2431" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2430" TEXT="Udemy practice tests (optional)" LINK="https://www.udemy.com/course/claude-developer/"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://www.udemy.com/course/claude-developer/</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2441" TEXT="10-30 · Read all notes/*.md end to end; re-read Exam Guide task statements …"><node ID="ID_2433" TEXT="Learn: Read all notes/*.md end to end; re-read Exam Guide task statements line by line"></node><node ID="ID_2437" TEXT="Build: One-page cheat sheet (for memory, not for the exam)"><node ID="ID_2434" TEXT="Read every notes file in order; merge anything missing into the Cheat sheet tab's lines in My notes."></node><node ID="ID_2435" TEXT="Print the Cheat sheet tab; read it twice today."></node><node ID="ID_2436" TEXT="Clear all due traps in Trap review; then run 'Review everything' once."></node></node><node ID="ID_2438" TEXT="✔ Done when: Cheat sheet printed; all traps in box 3 or higher."></node><node ID="ID_2440" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2439" TEXT="notes/*.md; the Cheat sheet tab of this tracker"></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2448" TEXT="10-31 · Practice exam #4 (timed) — must be 80%+"><node ID="ID_2442" TEXT="Learn: Practice exam #4 (timed) — must be 80%+"></node><node ID="ID_2446" TEXT="Build: Final weak-spot review"><node ID="ID_2443" TEXT="Fourth fresh set; timed; enter scores (Practice exam 4)."></node><node ID="ID_2444" TEXT="Decision point: if overall &lt; 80% or any domain &lt; 70%, reschedule the exam now (see trap below) rather than sit it."></node><node ID="ID_2445" TEXT="Otherwise: 30 minutes on the weakest domain's traps and stop."></node></node><node ID="ID_2447" TEXT="✔ Done when: Go / no-go decision made and recorded in My notes."></node></node><node ID="ID_2458" TEXT="11-01 · Light day: 20 questions max, then stop"><node ID="ID_2449" TEXT="Learn: Light day: 20 questions max, then stop"></node><node ID="ID_2454" TEXT="Build: Prepare room: clean desk, ID ready, webcam and mic tested, OnVUE app installed"><node ID="ID_2450" TEXT="20 mixed questions from the Question bank; stop regardless of score."></node><node ID="ID_2451" TEXT="Room: clear desk, one monitor, no papers, door closes; ID within reach; phone will be out of reach."></node><node ID="ID_2452" TEXT="Re-run the OnVUE system test; install/update the OnVUE app; charge the laptop; note the check-in link."></node><node ID="ID_2453" TEXT="Set two alarms; plan a 09:00 breakfast."></node></node><node ID="ID_2455" TEXT="✔ Done when: Room ready; system test passed; alarms set."></node><node ID="ID_2457" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_2456" TEXT="OnVUE requirements" LINK="https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://www.pearsonvue.com/us/en/anthropic.html</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2464" TEXT="11-02 · Rest. Skim traps only. Sleep early."><node ID="ID_2459" TEXT="Learn: Rest. Skim traps only. Sleep early."></node><node ID="ID_2462" TEXT="Build: Check-in link and ID on the desk"><node ID="ID_2460" TEXT="10 minutes: skim the Cheat sheet tab. No new material."></node><node ID="ID_2461" TEXT="Check-in link, ID and water on the desk. Sleep by 22:30."></node></node><node ID="ID_2463" TEXT="✔ Done when: You feel bored of the material — that is the goal."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2477" TEXT="📖 Study material"><node ID="ID_2476" TEXT="Exam-day tactics"><node ID="ID_2466" TEXT="53 questions in 120 min ≈ 2 min 15 s each. Flag anything over 3 min and move on;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>53 questions in 120 min ≈ 2 min 15 s each. Flag anything over 3 min and move on; review flagged at the end. Budget: first pass 75 min, review 30 min, spare 15.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2467" TEXT="Multiple-response items state how many to pick — count before you submit."></node><node ID="ID_2468" TEXT="Scenario questions reward the Anthropic-recommended answer: smallest adequate model,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Scenario questions reward the Anthropic-recommended answer: smallest adequate model, clear instructions before clever tricks, cache before batch before downgrade, structured tools over text parsing, workflow before agent, human approval before destructive actions, external content is untrusted, secrets never in prompts, simplest architecture first, evals before tuning.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2469" TEXT="Eliminate answers that solve a different problem (temperature for length, streaming…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Eliminate answers that solve a different problem (temperature for length, streaming for cost, batch for chat, bigger model for a prompt problem).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2470" TEXT="Read code snippets slowly — several questions turn on one field name (stop_reason,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Read code snippets slowly — several questions turn on one field name (stop_reason, tool_use_id, cache_control, tool_choice, max_tokens, budget_tokens).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2471" TEXT="&quot;Most cost-effective&quot; → caching / batch / Haiku. &quot;Most reliable structure&quot; → forced…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>&quot;Most cost-effective&quot; → caching / batch / Haiku. &quot;Most reliable structure&quot; → forced tool or structured outputs. &quot;Shared with the team&quot; → project scope / committed file. &quot;Must always happen&quot; → hook. &quot;Unknown number of steps&quot; → agent / orchestrator.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2472" TEXT="Check-in 10:00, start 10:30 IST. Nothing on the desk but ID; phone out of reach; no…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Check-in 10:00, start 10:30 IST. Nothing on the desk but ID; phone out of reach; no second monitor; no one enters the room.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2475" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2473" TEXT="If practice scores are below 80% on 31 Oct: reschedule — the exam guide requires at least 24 hours' notice, so the decision must be made by the morning of 2 Nov."></node><node ID="ID_2474" TEXT="A fail costs USD 125 and a 14-day wait (30 after a second fail, 90 after a third; max four attempts in 12 months)."></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2486" TEXT="❓ Self-check"><node ID="ID_2479" TEXT="Question says 'select TWO'. Habit?"><node ID="ID_2478" TEXT="→ Count your selections before submitting; multiple-response items lose credit for wrong counts."></node></node><node ID="ID_2481" TEXT="A question stem says 'most cost-effective'. Which answers are usually right?"><node ID="ID_2480" TEXT="→ Caching a stable prefix, Batches for offline work, or a smaller model that passes the eval."></node></node><node ID="ID_2483" TEXT="Stem says 'must always run'. Which mechanism?"><node ID="ID_2482" TEXT="→ A hook (enforcement), not CLAUDE.md (guidance)."></node></node><node ID="ID_2485" TEXT="Stem says 'unknown number of steps'. Architecture?"><node ID="ID_2484" TEXT="→ Agent (or orchestrator–workers) rather than a fixed workflow."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2491" TEXT="⚠ Traps to drill"><node ID="ID_2488" TEXT="Time per question?"><node ID="ID_2487" TEXT="→ ≈2 min 15 s; flag at 3 min; first pass 75 min, review 30."></node></node><node ID="ID_2490" TEXT="Reschedule rule?"><node ID="ID_2489" TEXT="→ If practice &lt; 80% on 31 Oct, reschedule ≥24 h before the appointment; a fail = USD 125 + 14-day wait (then 30, then 90; max 4 attempts/12 months)."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2495" TEXT="🗒 Cheat sheet"><node ID="ID_2492" TEXT="Answer keys: cheapest → cache/batch/Haiku · structure → forced tool/schema · team-shared → project scope · must-always → hook · unknown steps → agent · external content → untrusted · destructive → approve first"></node><node ID="ID_2493" TEXT="Eliminate wrong-problem answers: temperature≠length, streaming≠cost, batch≠chat, bigger model≠prompt fix"></node><node ID="ID_2494" TEXT="2:15 per question; flag at 3 min; count selections on multi-response"></node></node><node ID="ID_2502" TEXT="☑ Chapter checklist"><node ID="ID_2496" TEXT="Official Partner Academy prep course completed"></node><node ID="ID_2497" TEXT="Three consecutive practice exams at 80% or above"></node><node ID="ID_2498" TEXT="Every domain individually above 75%"></node><node ID="ID_2499" TEXT="All eight notes files reviewed twice"></node><node ID="ID_2500" TEXT="Room, ID, webcam, mic and OnVUE app verified the day before"></node><node ID="ID_2501" TEXT="Alarm set: check-in 10:00 IST on Tue 3 Nov"></node></node></node>
